// Node.js doesn't have Blobs. Instead, Node.js handles raw binary data using something called a Buffer.
// When your React app fires { type: "shape:new" } over the internet, it travels through the wires as
// electricity (zeros and ones). When it hits your Node.js server, the ws library hands it to your callback
// function exactly as it arrived: as a raw binary Buffer.

// IF it were express it implicitly handles these binary data like gatekeeper


